# PR Review Correction Loop (Pre-Merge)

Merge to `main` only when **blocking CI is green** and **automated review feedback has reached quiescence** (no new actionable bot comments on the latest pushed commit).

Complements `@.cursor/rules/011-coderabbit-pr-gate.mdc` (scope) and `@.cursor/rules/012-dependabot-pr-gate.mdc` (Dependabot).

## Bots in scope (address every actionable item)

| Source | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| **CodeRabbit** (`coderabbitai`) | Inline threads + **review body** (out-of-diff findings often appear only in the summary) |
| **CodeAnt** (`codeant-ai`) | Inline suggestions + quality-gate status contexts |
| **Copilot** (`copilot-pull-request-reviewer`) | Inline PR review comments |
| **DeepSource** (`deepsource-io`) | Inline threads when JS analyzer enabled in dashboard; `DeepSource: JavaScript` GitHub check disappears when dashboard analyzer is off (TOML has no `javascript` block) — see `docs/deepsource-javascript-ci.md`. Docker/Shell remain advisory. ESLint + `deploy.yml` are authoritative for TS/TSX. |
| **Socket Security** | Actionable PR alerts when they block merge |
| **Cursor Bugbot** | When explicitly requested |
| **Greptile / Codex** | Skip when trial or usage limits return no review (document in PR disposition comment) |

Human review comments requesting concrete fixes are in scope while open.

## Merge gate order (strict)

1. **Push** fix commits to the PR branch.
2. **Wait** for blocking CI on the latest commit (`deploy.yml` Typecheck/Lint/Tests, build, security audit — read job logs, not badge alone for advisory jobs).
3. **Collect** all open review threads (GraphQL `reviewThreads`) and scan latest bot **review bodies** for new actionable items.
4. **Fix or reply** on every thread; **resolve** threads after fix or documented rationale.
5. **Re-check** after CodeRabbit (or other bots) finish on the new commit — temporary rate limits may delay reviews **14–20+ minutes**; wait and re-poll before declaring quiescence. **Do not merge** while CodeRabbit `CHANGES_REQUESTED` targets an older commit or while unresolved inline threads remain.
6. **Merge** only when step 2 is green and step 5 shows no new actionable items.

Do **not** merge on stale bot approval from an older commit while newer commits are untested or unreviewed.

Do **not** use `git commit --no-verify` / `git push --no-verify` to skip Husky — pre-commit runs `typecheck`; pre-push runs `check:fast`. Bypassing hooks lets TypeScript errors reach CI after push.

## Correction loop (per finding)

1. Verify against **current** code on the PR branch (bots often comment on superseded commits).
2. **Fix** if valid; prefer minimal, focused diffs.
3. **Defer** only with a short English reply on the thread (rare — security/correctness findings should be fixed).
4. **Reply** on the inline thread citing the fixing commit when applicable.
5. **Resolve** the review thread (GitHub “Resolve conversation”).
6. Post a **PR disposition comment** when closing a large batch (bot → action table).

## CI vs advisory checks

- **Blocking:** `deploy.yml` quality gates, Chromium E2E (`e2e.yml`), cross-browser E2E (`e2e-cross-browser.yml` — Firefox/WebKit/mobile Chrome), required branch protections, Socket when flagged blocking.
- **Advisory (default):** DeepSource JavaScript (`deepsourceJavaScriptAdvisory: true`), Claude Code skipped jobs on PRs without `@claude`.
- **Claude Code `action_required`:** Workflow triggered by `pull_request_review_comment` may show **Approve and run workflows** with zero jobs — GitHub workflow-approval gate, not a failed test. Job `if` still requires `@claude` in the comment body; approval alone does not run Claude on bot threads.

## Collection commands (agents / maintainers)

```bash
# Unresolved threads with author
gh api graphql -f query='query { repository(owner:"qnbs", name:"AI-Research-Orchestrator") { pullRequest(number:N) { reviewThreads(first:100) { nodes { id isResolved comments(last:1) { nodes { databaseId author { login } body } } } } } } }'

# Latest CodeRabbit review commit
gh api repos/qnbs/AI-Research-Orchestrator/pulls/N/reviews --jq '[.[]|select(.user.login=="coderabbitai[bot]")]|sort_by(.submitted_at)|.[-1]'
```

Replace `N` with the PR number. After fixes, resolve threads via GraphQL `resolveReviewThread` or the GitHub UI.

## Lessons (standing)

- **Align identifiers end-to-end:** UI label, external URL, export/PDF, and corpus keys must use the same resolved identifier (P1-5 lesson).
- **Canonical legacy keys win:** When `pmid` and `articleId` disagree, trust the canonical `pmid` string for maps and hydration.
- **Hydrate before validation:** Run `ensureGroundedClaim` / `ensureArticleIdentifiers` before corpus validation and Dexie upgrades; guard non-string legacy keys.
- **i18n for all identifier types:** Copy toast and ARIA labels must not hard-code “PMID” when DOI/arXiv/PMCID are copied.
- **DOI URLs:** Use `encodeURI` for `doi.org` paths (preserve `/`); do not `encodeURIComponent` the full DOI.
- **CodeRabbit re-reviews** each push — expect 2–4 correction rounds on medium PRs; budget time for rate-limit delays.
- **DeepSource noise:** JavaScript analyzer is off in the DeepSource dashboard; `.deepsource.toml` has no `javascript` block (`docs/deepsource-dashboard-off.md`). Do not churn code solely for advisory DeepSource JavaScript unless policy flips to blocking.

